From 18338396b42681ea597df71f73070ce7d39bc903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:44:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] chimera: replace the bring-up rig with a Revdi daemon

Turn the hardware probe into an owned production control session that follows the current Vino AKE, key whitening, nonce, per-head authentication, finalization, mode, arm, and video sequences. Add a dual-head daemon that discovers EDIDs, creates safe Revdi outputs, tracks compositor mode changes, pads and encodes coherent frames with the kernel codec, and submits them on the matching endpoint. Keep the standalone coldstart as a small session smoke test and extend the offline oracle to cover mode and arm builders.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
